What is the C++ code to sort an array of integers in descending order and then find the median value of the sorted array? Here is an example array: [8, 2, 5, 1, 9, 3]
To sort the array in descending order, you can use the following C++ code:
int arr[] = {8, 2, 5, 1, 9, 3};
int n = sizeof(arr) / sizeof(arr[0]);
sort(arr, arr + n, greater<int>());
This will sort the array in descending order.
To find the median value of the sorted array, you can use the following C++ code:
int median;
if(n % 2 == 0)
    median = (arr[n/2 - 1] + arr[n/2]) / 2;
else
    median = arr[n/2];
This will give you the median value of the sorted array.

output:
Here's the complete C++ code to sort the array in descending order and find the median value:
```
#include <iostream>
#include <algorithm>
using namespace std;
int main() {
    int arr[] = {8, 2, 5, 1, 9, 3};
    int n = sizeof(arr) / sizeof(arr[0]);
    // Sort the array in descending order
    sort(arr, arr + n, greater<int>());
    // Find the median value
    int median;
    if(n % 2 == 0)
        median = (arr[n/2 - 1] + arr[n/2]) / 2;
    else
        median = arr[n/2];
    // Output the sorted array and the median value
    cout << "Sorted array in descending order: ";
    for(int i = 0; i < n; i++)
        cout << arr[i] << " ";
    cout << endl << "Median value: " << median << endl;
    return 0;
}
```
Output:
```
Sorted array in descending order: 9 8 5 3 2 1 
Median value: 4
```

