What would be the JavaScript code to calculate the weight of a basket of fruits after a given number of days of dehydration, assuming a constant dehydration rate? 
For instance, if we have a basket of fruits weighing 1 kilogram, and we want to know its weight after 10 days of dehydration at a rate of 1% per day, we can use the following formula:
W2 = W1 * Math.pow((1 - R/100), T);
Where W1 is the initial weight of the fruits (1 kg in our case), R is the dehydration rate (1% per day), and T is the number of days (10 in our case).
So, the JavaScript code would be:
let initialWeight = 1; // kg
let dehydrationRate = 1; // % per day
let days = 10;
let finalWeight = initialWeight * Math.pow((1 - dehydrationRate/100), days);
console.log("The final weight of the fruits after " + days + " days is: " + finalWeight + " kg");

